From 93113d26f57e02d846e14a1addd3e0af17c726c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefane Fermigier <sf@abilian.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 21:57:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(charts): sunburst, treemap, waterfall and funnel drawn as
 in Office

ElixirOffice's, from their commits 8f3b4c4 (0.8.0, their #78 and #79)
and 6f67073 (0.9.0), with their node tests, less two: one checks their
wording of the regular extended-chart title, which ours says otherwise,
and one their Change Colors ribbon, not taken. A sunburst's levels are
read root first, each top-level branch takes the next accent, and its
labels read along the radius, shrunk, wrapped or hidden to fit. A
treemap is laid out squarified, with a header per branch. A waterfall
takes accents for increase, decrease and total, with that legend, and
a funnel's labels are white. Dragging an extended chart's data label,
which stopped the editor, is ignored.
